// for one PRN code — already accounting for the half-sine pulse shape
// and upsampling to the bladeRF's sample rate, exactly as your generator
// produces it. Nothing here synthesizes chips or applies pulse shaping;
// whatever samples you paste in are loaded as the matched-filter
// reference as-is.
//
// Format: interleaved I/Q floats, i.e. { I0, Q0, I1, Q1, ... }, matching
// cufftComplex's layout directly. If your template is real-valued only
// (typical for a simple BPSK/half-sine baseband pulse train with no
// quadrature component), just set every Q sample to 0.0f — the matched
// filter works correctly on a reference stored that way.
